<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs estimated Friday 90,000 -USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs estimated Friday 90,000 -USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estimated interior Iowa and</p>
<p>southern Minnesota hog receipts:</p>
<p>Fridays:  90,000   Wk ago: 95,000  Yr ago:  85,000</p>
<p>Saturday: 10,000   Wk ago: 11,000  Yr ago:  12,000</p>
<p>Estimates include generally about 65 percent Carcass Base Hogs. Barrows and gilts were steady to weak with midsession Thursday. Trade light-moderate. Demand, offerings moderate.</p>
<p>				  Country		   Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    56.50 -57.50	   57.50 -58.50</p>
<p>few				 56.00		    57.00</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs	    55.50 -57.50	   56.00 -58.50</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs	    55.50 -57.50	   56.00 -58.50</p>
<p>Sows:  1.00-3.00 lower.</p>
<p>US 1-3 300-500 lbs   43.00 -45.00	   45.00 -46.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	    45.00 -47.00	   46.00 -48.00</p>
<p>Compared last week:  Barrows and gilts mostly 1.50 lower.</p>
<p>Slaughter sows 1.00-2.00 lower.</p>
<p>Receipts this week estimated at  525,000 compared with 531,000 last week and 480,000 a year ago. Barrow and gilt average weight for week ending 19 July 1997 was 250.9 compared previous week 250.4 and 246.1 a year ago.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
